# BUGS

A file's token is made once and kept for the open file's life, so a token whose holds have run out becomes good again at the next `Tshare` of the file: anyone who kept it may join then.

`Tseek` and `Tdesc` cannot reach a directory, which has no open file, so a directory's offset stays the client's; a `Tseek` on one, like one on a fid with no open file, is answered `fid already in use`, a misleading string.

Of the servers with `posix`, the boot manifests give `entropy` only to `tmpfs`, `ptyd` and `fsd`; `dosfs`, `isofs` and `distd` refuse `Tshare`, so a child's descriptors on their files are opened again and do not share their parent's offset.
